+
+The service implements JSON CRUD at `/items` and `/items/:id`. IDs are
+lowercase URL-safe names, titles are trimmed strings of 1–80 characters, and
+`done` is boolean. POST defaults `done` to `false`; malformed requests return
+JSON errors. Mutations are serialized and atomically replace a versioned JSON
+store, creating parent directories as needed. Existing malformed stores are
+rejected synchronously by the factory. `onStage` is awaited immediately before
+replacement (`beforeCommit`) and after the replacement is durable
+(`afterCommit`), which can be used by fault-injection tests.
+
+Run the automated tests with:
+
+```text
+node --test test.cjs
+```
+
+Recovery is limited to one owning process, as specified: concurrent writers
+from multiple processes are outside scope. Atomic replacement ensures an
+interrupted write leaves the old or new complete store; temporary files are
+not used for recovery and never override the committed file.
