 # Persistent REST item service

-Implementation and self-test documentation goes here.
+`api.cjs` exports `createServer({ file, onStage })`. It validates an existing
+JSON store synchronously and returns an unbound `node:http` server; the caller
+owns `listen()` and `close()`. The store has the form `{version: 1, items: []}`.
+Missing parent directories and a missing file are created on the first durable
+mutation. Items are validated, writes are serialized and atomically replaced,
+and successful mutation responses are sent only after the replacement is
+durable. `onStage` is awaited at `beforeCommit` and `afterCommit`.
+
+Supported routes are `GET /items`, `GET /items/:id`, `POST /items`,
+`PATCH /items/:id`, and `DELETE /items/:id`. JSON errors use `{error: string}`.
+IDs match `/^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$/`; titles are trimmed to 1–80 characters.
+
+Run the self-test with `node --test test.cjs`.
+
+Recovery is limited to a single owning process. Atomic replacement preserves
+the previous or complete new store if interrupted; temporary files are not
+used for recovery and do not override the committed file. Cross-process
+simultaneous writers are outside the API contract.
